  "body": "## Change\n\nCumulative HRM completion candidate retaining the accepted dormant reconciliation/roster work and read-only partial schema exporter. This slice removes private caught values from request submit, decision, cancellation and optional Route-entitlement logging. Three finite error labels and one dedicated warning label preserve response, auth, idempotency, notification and domain-service behavior. Entitlement failure remains a warning and HRM decision proceeds with Route enrichment disabled.\n\nAccepted head `ef5d90010d9b317a493dfe7ae574b1863f3c83fb`, tree `5b94c2111dbe51ceb74b1e803e142fff74e66cbc`, parent `2c5a6a4b35cb96988f9f3c417b122d788498c3a7`. Fresh main `86cba428d39e3ce4be13245bdb8e34e49dccf8d4`; synthetic `7b517816410e29d84a03f368954541ca180b79f6` has the same tree. Six-path slice; Support592 and applied migrations/baselines unchanged.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Owner:76 focused tests PASS (27 new handler cases,16 privacy variants),225 MTM/capability/isolation regressions PASS; lint and bounded production typecheck PASS.\n- Independent:57 tests PASS, all8762blobs/modes verified,6-path delta/8756unchanged parent blobs; exact-source and hosted review accepted without unresolved findings.\n- Hosted exact head:5 mandatory+6 additional checks PASS, all9workflows successful on attempt1. Optional production build SKIPPED. Restore safeJSON:15uniquePASS,2cleanupPASS,10authentication records,34source bindings independently verified.\n- [Final evidence archive](https://github.com/rashadoni/leaddrive-v2/tree/c3e196a14e56c16d038ff58fda036f9c9425e30e/docs/evidence/workforce-request-safe-logging-2026-10-06):42files read back byte-exact. Independent terminal receipt SHA256 `c6fb9ac26988a7b1c173423646c17e63018a75303e3593f969ae3512b403c67c`.\n- Test-inclusive compiler retains exactly2historicalTS2737 in sharedMTMmock, byte-identical to main/parent. Isolated reproduction:ES2017 rejects1n; BigInt(1) compiles and preserves value. This separate sharedfixture correction is diagnosed, not hidden by changing a target or baseline.\n- Initial new-test missing brace and omitted normal next-auth augmentation in the local bounded config were corrected; original failures retained. Hosted64file/code and18known-test baselines unchanged; no globally clean compiler/zero failed-suite claim.\n- Handler tests mock auth wrappers/domain services/Prisma; no end-to-end auth/localPG claim. Only restore safeJSON was inspected; five other browser payloads remain metadata-only. Prior source/restore history preserved.\n\n## Canonical criteria and finite next work\n\nWF-C10-011 stays PLANNED: four more private error paths now have canary coverage, but complete source/alias/shared/framework scan and analytics/dashboard destination review remain required.\n\nWF-C12-002 stays PARTIAL: finite labels advance the no-high-cardinality criterion; end-to-end cardinality/privacy, collection/dashboard ingestion, approved paging/SLO and delivery remain unproven.\n\nRemaining direct calls:45raw+1name-derived in finite batches4Today/timesheet/exceptions,9attendance,33configuration. The prepared next batch preserves typed Today suppressed-log and timesheet409 branches. After these batches, consolidate coverage/destination evidence once; close only the whole canonical criterion, otherwise name the exact operational blocker and move to independent fault/fairness and entitlement-matrix work.\n\nLedger82/161DONE,79open,weighted59%; C12-008PARTIAL. Historical api_keys provenance stays with the separate backup owner. No migration/baseline/grant/credential edit, Support change, Contabo/SSH/Mac action, merge, deployment or runtime activation occurred.\n",
